WEBVTT

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:21.820
Gion-kun... Gion-kun... We're here.

00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:28.710
All right!

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:31.070
We're in Sugadaira!

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:33.720
You slept the whole way from school.

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:36.010
Nearly four hours straight...

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:25.010
<b>Episode 17    Summer Training Camp</b>

00:02:21.010 --> 00:02:24.730
Wow, there are dudes in 
all kinds of jerseys here.

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:28.330
High school teams from all over the country
come here for their summer training camp.

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:30.750
A lot of college students turn up, too.

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:32.880
That's amazing!

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:35.210
There's even a rugby shop!

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:36.890
That's not the only one.

00:02:37.310 --> 00:02:40.910
There are tons of rugby shops in Sugadaira.

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:43.160
Wow, awesome!

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:44.020
And...

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:45.110
And?

00:02:45.110 --> 00:02:46.890
They even have gift shops.

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:49.520
Yeah, I'm sure they do...

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:54.820
This intersection is the heart of Sugadaira.

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:56.480
Really?

00:02:56.480 --> 00:03:00.380
<b>Match Schedule</b>

00:02:56.950 --> 00:03:00.380
The matches scheduled for 
the day are written up here.

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:01.750
Hey, they really are...

00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:03.090
Look, it's Sagami!

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:04.620
They've got a game today.

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:06.530
So they are.

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:10.340
If we get lucky with our schedule, 
we might get to see some other schools play.

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:12.750
Hey, we're going to leave you behind.

00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:16.910
How far is the inn?

00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:18.590
About fifteen minutes away.

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:20.250
Keep walking, everyone!

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:33.400
<b>Ikuta Inn</b>

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:32.450
We're broke, so the inn's kinda run down.

00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:33.400
Hoakari, you...

00:03:34.220 --> 00:03:35.100
Good.

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:35.650
What?

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:39.780
Swanky hotels are too good for kids.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:41.690
This is just right.

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:48.660
You must be from Kanagawa High.

00:03:49.130 --> 00:03:51.560
Huh? Who are you? The coach?

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:52.860
Thank you for having us.

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:55.670
We'll be staying here for the next five days.

00:03:56.060 --> 00:04:00.210
No, thank you for staying with us.

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:02.180
Y-Yes, sir.

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:03.440
Is something wrong?

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:05.870
Well, actually...

00:04:05.870 --> 00:04:08.830
Every year, our students are badly behaved.

00:04:08.830 --> 00:04:12.100
Last year, the third-years 
caused a lot of trouble.

00:04:21.140 --> 00:04:23.070
It'll be fine this year.

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:24.530
What?

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:27.080
Show us to our rooms.

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:29.450
We have a match at two today.

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:33.790
We'll be heading straight over to the field 
once we've dropped off our things.

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:35.170
What?

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:36.950
Straight over to the field?

00:04:36.950 --> 00:04:38.750
But it's still only 11...

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:40.630
Yes, straight over to the field.

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:45.960
Put your things in your rooms 
and get changed.

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:48.010
We'll be running to the field.

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:49.010
What?

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:50.010
What?

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:52.330
What?!

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:53.020
<b>Ikuta Inn</b>

00:04:56.660 --> 00:04:59.650
Okay, that's warmed you up a little.

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:08.920
Um, normally, we have lunch at the inn...

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:12.850
Lunch? We gave them theirs on the bus.

00:05:12.850 --> 00:05:16.170
What? But it's, uh...

00:05:17.270 --> 00:05:18.170
Komori-san.

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:22.550
What drill are we doing for practice?

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:25.550
Running passes for one hour.

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:27.550
Yes, sir!

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:30.010
Bingo! We always do that.

00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:31.860
Ume-chan, balls!

00:05:31.860 --> 00:05:33.180
Gotcha.

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:34.280
Here.

00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:35.140
Here.

00:05:38.010 --> 00:05:39.920
The air here's so fresh!

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:40.980
It's hot, though.

00:05:41.350 --> 00:05:43.660
But it's refreshing, isn't it?

00:05:43.660 --> 00:05:44.760
Yeah.

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:47.100
It's not so humid in the highlands.

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:50.620
This is so fun!

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:52.620
Pass the ball, you little turd!

00:05:53.030 --> 00:05:55.070
The grass is nice.

00:05:55.070 --> 00:05:58.500
It feels great!

00:05:58.950 --> 00:06:01.880
Sensei, did you put on sunscreen?

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:03.450
Oh, no...

00:06:03.450 --> 00:06:06.720
If you don't, you'll burn.

00:06:07.150 --> 00:06:10.170
Are you going to watch them play this year?

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:12.590
Uh, yeah.

00:06:12.590 --> 00:06:15.100
Awesome. I could use some help.

00:06:19.590 --> 00:06:20.850
Huh?

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:23.630
Where are the Kanagawa students?

00:06:23.630 --> 00:06:27.370
Huh? They headed to the field 
right after checking in.

00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:29.780
What? Without having lunch?

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:34.620
Yeah. If they come inside covered 
in mud again, I'll kick them out.

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:39.620
But I've brought them dessert. 
What should I do with this now?

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:44.130
Okay, take five.

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:48.880
It's so hot...

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:50.520
I'm dying.

00:06:53.530 --> 00:06:58.540
Our opponent today is 
Tenjiku Technical School from Osaka.

00:06:59.130 --> 00:07:02.060
The team itself is relatively new.

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:03.880
But they've produced results.

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:07.010
Last year, they made it to the Osaka quarters.

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:10.180
Osaka is a competitive region.

00:07:10.180 --> 00:07:13.570
As a first opponent, they might 
cause us some problems.

00:07:14.230 --> 00:07:16.090
It's 12:50 right now.

00:07:16.590 --> 00:07:21.210
They've probably finished eating 
and are coming here to warm up.

00:07:22.190 --> 00:07:25.050
While they were lounging around for an hour,

00:07:25.050 --> 00:07:29.050
you guys were here doing running passes 
until you were drenched in sweat.

00:07:29.980 --> 00:07:31.230
They're a strong team.

00:07:31.710 --> 00:07:37.680
But at the very least, in the past hour, 
the gap between us has closed a little.

00:07:38.740 --> 00:07:40.280
Have confidence in yourselves.

00:07:40.280 --> 00:07:42.030
Remember what I told you yesterday?

00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:43.810
The result...

00:07:44.200 --> 00:07:46.040
We're playing Kanagawa.

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:47.320
What're they like?

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:50.030
...is decided before the game even starts.

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:52.700
Huh?

00:07:54.350 --> 00:07:55.760
There're people here.

00:07:55.760 --> 00:07:59.220
Looks like they're in 
the middle of a session.

00:07:59.220 --> 00:08:01.460
Maybe they're the guys who played before us.

00:08:02.330 --> 00:08:04.000
We're going to win!

00:08:04.430 --> 00:08:05.680
Captain.

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:06.750
We're going to win.

00:08:07.100 --> 00:08:09.990
We're a winning team.

00:08:09.990 --> 00:08:13.720
All right! Let's do some more running passes!

00:08:14.150 --> 00:08:17.240
Let's become even more of a winning team!

00:08:17.240 --> 00:08:19.340
Gion-kun, you can barely stand.

00:08:19.340 --> 00:08:21.480
You need to rest.

00:08:22.290 --> 00:08:25.600
Um, I'm from Ikuta Inn.

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:29.720
I heard you'd gone off to practice 
without having any lunch first...

00:08:29.720 --> 00:08:32.240
Would you like some dessert, at least?

00:08:38.650 --> 00:08:40.740
We would, thank you.

00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:44.330
All right!

00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:54.260
Your name's Miki-chan? How old are you?

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:58.260
Sixteen. I started helping my uncle this year.

00:08:58.620 --> 00:09:02.280
Once we're finished eating, 
let's start practicing again!

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:05.630
What's their deal?

00:09:09.430 --> 00:09:12.540
Are we there yet?

00:09:12.540 --> 00:09:14.800
The field's right there.

00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:16.280
It's so hot...

00:09:16.690 --> 00:09:17.720
Who are they playing?

00:09:17.720 --> 00:09:22.080
Tenjiku Tech. They made it to
the Osaka quarters last year.

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:24.910
Our schedule's been kind to us.

00:09:24.910 --> 00:09:28.670
<b>Todo-dai Sagami</b>

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:28.020
We get to see Jinko's first match.

00:09:31.060 --> 00:09:34.410
'Sup, I'm Tenjiku's captain, Sano.

00:09:34.410 --> 00:09:37.960
I'm the vice-captain, Osaka Sunao.
Nice to meet ya.

00:09:37.960 --> 00:09:40.490
They're speaking in Kansai accents...

00:09:40.490 --> 00:09:41.770
I'm scared...

00:09:41.770 --> 00:09:43.100
Hey now!

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:46.790
I'm Jinko's captain, Sekizan.

00:09:46.790 --> 00:09:49.400
I'm the vice-captain, Hachioji.

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:50.360
Nice to meet you.

00:09:53.850 --> 00:09:55.830
Anyways, nice meetin' you guys.

00:10:01.420 --> 00:10:04.200
Their captain's hair is seriously whack.

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:06.730
Take a look at Jinko's coach.

00:10:06.730 --> 00:10:08.420
He's an old fogey!

00:10:12.140 --> 00:10:14.530
Tenjiku seems boorish.

00:10:14.530 --> 00:10:15.920
You're one to talk.

00:10:16.450 --> 00:10:17.280
Hori.

00:10:17.280 --> 00:10:18.270
Yeah?

00:10:18.270 --> 00:10:20.590
Does Tenjiku have any famous players?

00:10:21.150 --> 00:10:25.970
I know all the noteworthy 
players in Kanagawa.

00:10:25.970 --> 00:10:27.670
Nerd.

00:10:27.670 --> 00:10:30.530
But even I haven't researched Osaka...

00:10:31.020 --> 00:10:34.880
...which is what I'd like to say,
 but they do have one.

00:10:34.880 --> 00:10:40.370
A player who made the 
All-Osaka team in middle school.

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:41.320
Really?

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:44.200
Your hair's nuts, man!

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:47.200
Can I touch it? Can I?

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:50.860
I really wanna touch it. Can I?

00:10:50.860 --> 00:10:54.660
Suna-chan, you're bein' rude. Stop that.

00:10:54.660 --> 00:10:57.380
But, Hosoyan, isn't it super cool?

00:10:58.090 --> 00:11:00.090
It <i>is</i> super cool...

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:04.910
Hosoyan, your front teeth are 
stickin' out more than usual.

00:11:05.910 --> 00:11:08.130
See? He's laughin' at ya.

00:11:08.130 --> 00:11:10.870
Sorry, we're a little nervous.

00:11:10.870 --> 00:11:13.230
Let's have some fun.

00:11:13.800 --> 00:11:15.980
Quit jokin' around, Sunao.

00:11:16.300 --> 00:11:19.760
The backs need to talk. Hurry up, dingus.

00:11:19.760 --> 00:11:22.380
And Hosotani, the forwards 
are in a huddle over there.

00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:23.580
What're you playin' at?

00:11:23.580 --> 00:11:25.990
Renpei, we're sorry. We'll be right there.

00:11:28.840 --> 00:11:32.040
I wanted to play a better-known team.

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:33.750
Who the hell is Jinko, anyways?

00:11:33.750 --> 00:11:35.430
Hey, Renpei!

00:11:35.430 --> 00:11:36.750
Anyhow, nice meetin' you guys.

00:11:39.180 --> 00:11:41.510
Sakura Renpei, third-year.

00:11:41.510 --> 00:11:45.510
During his third year of middle school, 
he was the Osaka team's star fullback.

00:11:45.900 --> 00:11:48.620
His kicking and running abilities
were exceptional.

00:11:48.620 --> 00:11:51.190
You've sure done your research.

00:11:51.190 --> 00:11:54.280
Sounds like a tough first opponent for Jinko.

00:11:54.280 --> 00:11:56.900
I don't know if they're lucky or unlucky.

00:11:57.550 --> 00:12:01.990
I'm the Tenjiku rugby team coach, Futami.

00:12:02.550 --> 00:12:04.350
Nice to meet you.

00:12:04.350 --> 00:12:07.550
I'm the Jinko rugby team coach, Komori.

00:12:07.550 --> 00:12:08.570
Nice to meet you.

00:12:12.220 --> 00:12:13.420
Okay.

00:12:14.350 --> 00:12:16.450
Here's our starting lineup.

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:21.010
<b>Jelly</b>

00:12:19.020 --> 00:12:21.010
<b>There's one left...</b>

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:24.010
<b>Who wants more...</b>

00:12:28.990 --> 00:12:30.640
Kifune, you're starting.

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:31.490
What?

00:12:31.490 --> 00:12:32.750
You can do it.

00:12:33.950 --> 00:12:35.260
Kifune, huh?

00:12:35.260 --> 00:12:36.520
That's different.

00:12:37.810 --> 00:12:40.780
You guys know what to do.

00:12:41.370 --> 00:12:44.070
Don't give anything less than 100%.

00:12:45.890 --> 00:12:48.780
I've got nothing else to say. Now, go.

00:12:48.780 --> 00:12:49.890
Yes, sir!

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:54.460
It's starting.

00:12:54.460 --> 00:12:56.900
Sensei, let me hear you cheering for them.

00:12:56.900 --> 00:12:57.740
What?

00:12:57.740 --> 00:12:59.750
Go, Jinko!

00:12:59.750 --> 00:13:00.920
Go!

00:13:05.430 --> 00:13:06.720
Yeah!

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:10.970
Why're you unknowns tryin' so hard?

00:13:10.970 --> 00:13:12.310
It's obnoxious!

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:19.250
What a kick.

00:13:19.250 --> 00:13:22.320
Forty meters. No... more?

00:13:22.660 --> 00:13:24.090
Seriously?

00:13:24.090 --> 00:13:25.720
Get back there!

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:33.540
Kifune, kick it as hard as you can!

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:34.520
Yes, sir.

00:13:42.900 --> 00:13:45.780
That's only half as far as Tenjiku's kick.

00:13:45.780 --> 00:13:48.290
They've got a different 
fullback playing today.

00:13:48.290 --> 00:13:49.850
You can do it, Jinko.

00:14:00.220 --> 00:14:01.290
Another kick?

00:14:01.290 --> 00:14:03.900
Backs, get back there!

00:14:12.470 --> 00:14:15.780
Jinko's kicks have been no great shakes.

00:14:24.570 --> 00:14:26.630
Tenjiku's ball. Line out!

00:14:33.690 --> 00:14:36.850
<i>Should I have kicked that out?</i>

00:14:37.660 --> 00:14:38.810
Huh...

00:14:39.170 --> 00:14:43.030
Renpei, you're playin' well today. 
They're really soarin' off your cleat!

00:14:43.030 --> 00:14:44.870
Jinko's shocked by—

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:45.200
Leave me alone, Sunao.

00:14:45.200 --> 00:14:46.740
You're annoyin'.

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:02.420
Tenjiku's forwards are big.

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:05.720
Their #4, Inafune, in 189 centimeters tall.

00:15:06.190 --> 00:15:07.940
Where did you get that information?

00:15:08.360 --> 00:15:11.070
The official Tenjiku rugby team website.

00:15:11.070 --> 00:15:15.170
Their #14, Oshima, is also 180 
centimeters, despite being a winger.

00:15:15.830 --> 00:15:19.720
So they focus on aerial battles because 
they're so good at punting the ball long.

00:15:24.190 --> 00:15:28.940
Toru, nice kick! Let's go for it!

00:15:31.530 --> 00:15:32.360
Matsu-san!

00:15:38.280 --> 00:15:40.910
Their #10 ain't a bad kicker...

00:15:41.420 --> 00:15:42.790
Renpei!

00:15:50.280 --> 00:15:51.620
What kind of catch was that?

00:15:51.620 --> 00:15:53.370
He's not taking them seriously at all.

00:15:53.370 --> 00:15:56.640
Jinko's fullback is good.

00:15:56.640 --> 00:15:57.560
What?

00:15:57.560 --> 00:15:58.770
Kibi.

00:16:00.220 --> 00:16:05.180
As another fullback, what do you 
think of Kifune's movements?

00:16:05.180 --> 00:16:07.150
Uh, well...

00:16:10.580 --> 00:16:12.460
His positioning is good.

00:16:13.770 --> 00:16:16.070
He knows where the ball's gonna drop.

00:16:16.070 --> 00:16:17.770
He doesn't waste energy running around.

00:16:17.770 --> 00:16:21.450
And his kicks aren't particularly long...

00:16:21.810 --> 00:16:25.030
...but they land in awkward places.

00:16:25.030 --> 00:16:28.970
They can't be caught
without letting them bounce first.

00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:35.220
Sakura Renpei's kicks and catches 
are flashy, and he's certainly good.

00:16:35.960 --> 00:16:39.720
But the truly skilled fullback
 playing in this game is...

00:16:40.720 --> 00:16:43.240
Everything about him is just so plain.

00:16:43.240 --> 00:16:45.730
His actions, his personality, 
even his existence...

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:47.030
You're right.

00:16:47.630 --> 00:16:51.360
It took me a while to
notice his strengths, too.

00:16:51.820 --> 00:16:55.450
Fullbacks are the last line of defense
before the goal line.

00:16:55.450 --> 00:17:00.200
I wanted to try using
his plain but solid play.

00:17:00.700 --> 00:17:03.370
You've been paying attention 
to your surroundings, too.

00:17:03.370 --> 00:17:07.610
Dammit! I hate to admit it, but it's true.

00:17:07.610 --> 00:17:11.130
Once the game's over, 
I'm going to pick his brain.

00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:11.130
Plain is good

00:17:16.580 --> 00:17:18.340
Knock-on by Tenjiku!

00:17:18.920 --> 00:17:23.350
Yo. Change of plan. Tell Renpei.

00:17:35.990 --> 00:17:37.740
They got the ball!

00:17:38.590 --> 00:17:39.910
Seriously?!

00:17:40.260 --> 00:17:42.910
Tenjiku's hooker is good.

00:17:43.890 --> 00:17:45.410
Run!

00:17:49.030 --> 00:17:51.430
Jinko sure go for the low blows!

00:17:52.510 --> 00:17:56.130
But if they don't hit you, who cares?

00:17:56.130 --> 00:17:57.430
Sunao!

00:17:57.820 --> 00:17:59.180
Give me the ball.

00:17:59.180 --> 00:18:00.300
Renpei!

00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:06.560
Renpei, you know what to do!

00:18:07.700 --> 00:18:09.060
I know.

00:18:18.090 --> 00:18:19.110
He's good!

00:18:19.110 --> 00:18:22.060
They noticed Jinko's #15.

00:18:22.060 --> 00:18:24.120
They've stopped the long-range kicks.

00:18:26.120 --> 00:18:29.370
Renpei, pass the ball!

00:18:29.980 --> 00:18:30.950
Renpe—

00:18:35.610 --> 00:18:37.170
What?!

00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:04.180
I can't believe he made the ball stop
right on the goal-line.

00:19:04.180 --> 00:19:05.870
He really is a good kicker, isn't he?

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:09.300
I told you not to kick, Renpei.

00:19:09.300 --> 00:19:11.250
Who cares? It worked.

00:19:11.250 --> 00:19:13.380
Renpei, nice kickin'.

00:19:13.730 --> 00:19:16.760
A line-out five meters from Jinko's goal-line.

00:19:16.760 --> 00:19:19.630
Jinko's in trouble already.

00:19:20.010 --> 00:19:25.760
Why did he kick the ball out after 
it stopped just before crossing the line?

00:19:25.760 --> 00:19:26.810
You idiot.

00:19:26.810 --> 00:19:30.520
We can't contest it right in front of goal
with only a few guys behind the ball.

00:19:30.520 --> 00:19:32.690
Even if we're now basically 
handing them the ball,

00:19:32.690 --> 00:19:36.140
it's still safer to go for the line-out
so the entire team can get back and defend.

00:19:36.620 --> 00:19:37.780
Oh, I get it.

00:19:38.300 --> 00:19:39.690
Two...

00:19:40.250 --> 00:19:41.100
One...

00:19:42.190 --> 00:19:44.120
I won't let them have the ball!

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:44.990
Six!

00:19:48.620 --> 00:19:49.700
What? What's this?

00:19:49.700 --> 00:19:50.640
A wild throw?

00:19:50.640 --> 00:19:52.830
Did Iwashimizu's pressure get to him?

00:19:53.450 --> 00:19:55.500
No, this is...

00:19:57.670 --> 00:20:00.050
A long throw-in! Not good!

00:20:06.570 --> 00:20:08.060
You bastard!

00:20:13.820 --> 00:20:15.060
Try!

00:20:15.640 --> 00:20:20.850
Normally, they'd go for a try 
with a maul from the line-out...

00:20:21.380 --> 00:20:23.410
...but they went for the long throw instead.

00:20:23.890 --> 00:20:25.850
They outsmarted the defense.

00:20:27.070 --> 00:20:28.240
This is informative.

00:20:28.660 --> 00:20:30.500
Renpei, nice run.

00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:35.270
You guys can't score without me, can you?

00:20:35.270 --> 00:20:36.050
What?

00:20:36.050 --> 00:20:38.630
You're in my way. Get back there already.

00:20:38.630 --> 00:20:40.110
I'm ready to kick off.

00:20:40.110 --> 00:20:42.070
Renpei, nice try!

00:20:45.180 --> 00:20:47.680
Tenjiku

00:20:45.180 --> 00:20:47.680
Jinko

00:20:48.050 --> 00:20:50.060
Don't worry about it! Change gears!

00:20:50.550 --> 00:20:54.940
Jinko's staying calm. 
They're just getting started.

00:21:02.180 --> 00:21:02.900
Okay!

00:21:07.720 --> 00:21:09.200
Shinshi!

00:21:10.910 --> 00:21:11.730
Wow.

00:21:11.730 --> 00:21:13.810
Great tackle, but...

00:21:13.810 --> 00:21:16.210
Tenjiku's quick to follow up.

00:21:17.210 --> 00:21:19.210
They're already going for the ruck.

00:21:19.620 --> 00:21:21.370
Their prop, Oshima.

00:21:21.370 --> 00:21:24.220
184 centimeters. 100 kilograms.

00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:35.350
All right! We got the ball back!

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:37.620
That was amazing!

00:21:39.740 --> 00:21:42.290
Sumo wrestle here.

00:21:42.980 --> 00:21:44.600
Ready...

00:21:45.160 --> 00:21:46.990
That's it. That posture.

00:21:48.330 --> 00:21:49.810
That's the ruck posture.

00:21:50.620 --> 00:21:54.100
The lower player wins in a ruck.

00:21:54.100 --> 00:21:56.620
Start from that position and...

00:21:56.620 --> 00:21:57.370
Fight!

00:21:59.500 --> 00:22:03.130
Push your opponent up 
diagonally and flip him over.

00:22:03.830 --> 00:22:05.550
All right!

00:22:06.680 --> 00:22:10.270
<i>All right! The sumo wrestling's helping!</i>

00:22:12.570 --> 00:22:13.590
Good.

00:23:45.060 --> 00:23:50.070
<b>Next Time "Study"</b>

00:23:46.040 --> 00:23:48.250
Next time: "Study."
